  <language>fr_FR</language>
  <keyword>between</keyword>
  <short_description>Renvoie des durees calendaires entre deux valeurs datetime.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>c = between(t1, t2)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>c = between(t1, t2, components)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>inputs</param_name>
      <param_description>Deux entrees datetime ou compatibles date et un selecteur optionnel comme years, quarters, months ou days.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output</param_name>
      <param_description>Un tableau calendarDuration.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Renvoie des durees calendaires entre deux valeurs datetime.</p>
    <p>between exprime l intervalle avec des composants calendaires entiers et des restes jours/temps. La fonction supporte l expansion scalaire entre les bornes.</p>
    <p>Array-valued inputs keep their data shape when the operation supports arrays. Scalar operands are expanded where the implementation defines scalar expansion.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Utilisation de base.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[c = between(datetime(2024, 1, 15), datetime(2024, 3, 20))
split(c, 'months')
split(c, 'days')
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
